## EXPERIMENTAL PROCEDURES
## Synthesis of Au(III)-MOFs for Catalysis
IPrAu(III)Cl-IRMOF-10
To a 2 dram vial was added $\mathsf{I P r A u}(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{B P D C})\mathsf{C}\mathsf{I}$ $(8.6~\mathsf{m g}$ , 0.010 mmol, 0.25 equiv), ${\mathsf{H}}_{2}{\mathsf{B P D C}}$ $(7.3~\mathsf{m g}$ , 0.030 mmol, 0.75 equiv), $Z n(N O_{3})_{2}\cdot4+H_{2}O(42\ m g,0.16\ m m o l,$ 4.0 equiv), and diethyl formamide $(2.14\mathrm{mL})$ . The reaction mixture was capped, sonicated for 5 min, then heated at $90^{\circ}C$ in an oven for $24\mathsf{h}$ . This yielded yellow crystals, which were washed with DMF $\langle6\mathsf{m L}\times5\rangle$ ), DCM $\langle6\bmod{}\times15\rangle$ , then ${\mathsf{M e N O}}_{2}\left(6{\mathsf{m L}}\times5\right)$ . Due to a loss of crystallinity of IPrAu(III)Cl-IRMOF-10 in the absence of solvent, the crystals were immersed in solvent prior to ${\sf A g S b F}_{6}$ treatment. $16\%$ loading $\mathsf{I P r A u}(\mathsf{B P D C})\mathsf{C}\mathsf{I}$ versus BPDC was observed by digestion ${}^{1}\mathsf{H N M R}$ analysis. Zn:Au ratio of 88:12 observed by ICP-AES (expected Zn:Au ratio: 89:11).
## IPrAu(III)SbF6-IRMOF-10
To a $2m L$ vial was added IPrAu(III)Cl-IRMOF-10 $16\%\mathsf{I P r A u(B P D C)C l}$ loading, $2\mathsf{m g}$ , 1 equiv) immersed in ${\mathsf{M e N O}}_{2}$ $(0.1~\mathrm{mL})$ , followed by the addition of a solution of $\mathsf{A g S b F}_{6}$ $7~{\mathsf{m M}}$ in $\mathsf{M e N O}_{2},0.13\mathsf{m L}$ , 1 equiv). After $48\ h$ , the crystals were washed with ${\mathsf{M e N O}}_{2}$ $(2\ m L\times3)$ then DCM $(2~\mathsf{m L}\times5)$ . Due to a loss of crystallinity of IPrAu(III)SbF6-IRMOF-10 in the absence of solvent, the crystals were left immersed in solvent prior to catalysis.
## IPrAu(III)Cl-bio-MOF-100
To a 1 dram vial was added bio-MOF-100 $(20\ m\mathsf{g})$ ), $\mathsf{I P r A u(H_{2}B P D C)C l\ (20\ m g)}$ , and DMF $(0.9~\mathrm{mL})$ . The reaction mixture was capped, then heated at $50^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ in an oven for $96\mathrm{h}$ . This yielded colorless crystals, which were washed with DMF $\langle3\mathrm{mL}\times7\rangle$ , DCM $(3\mathrm{mL}\times15)$ , then ${\mathsf{M e N O}}_{2}$ $3\mathrm{mL}\times5)$ . Due to a loss of crystallinity of ${\mathsf{I P r A u}}({\mathsf{I I I}}){\mathsf{C}}{\mathsf{I}}$ -bioMOF-100 in the absence of solvent, the crystals were immersed in solvent prior to TlPF6 treatment. $15\%$ loading IPrAu(BPDC)Cl versus BPDC was observed by digestion $^1\mathsf{H}$ NMR. Zn:Au ratio of 89:11 observed by ICP-AES (expected Zn:Au ratio: 90:10).
## $I P r A u({I I I})P F_{6}$ -bio-MOF-100
To a $2m L$ vial was added IPrAu(III)Cl-bio-MOF-100 ( $15\%$ IPrAu(BPDC)Cl loading, $5\mathsf{m g}$ , 1 equiv) immersed in ${\mathsf{M e N O}}_{2}$ $(0.1~\mathrm{mL})$ , followed by the addition of a solution of ${\mathsf{T}}|{\mathsf{P}}{\mathsf{F}}_{6}$ ( $15~\mathsf{m M}$ in ${\mathsf{M e N O}}_{2}$ , $0.10\mathrm{ml}$ , 1 equiv). After $48\mathrm{~h~}$ , the crystals were washed
with ${\mathsf{M e N O}}_{2}$ $(2~\mathsf{m L}\times3)$ then $C H C l_{3}$ $(2~\mathsf{m L}\times5)$ . Due to a loss of crystallinity of $\mathsf{I P r A u(\mathsf{I I I})P F}_{6}$ -bio-MOF-100 in the absence of solvent, the crystals were left immersed in solvent prior to catalysis.
General Procedures for Catalysis with Au(III)-MOFs IPrAu(III)SbF6-IRMOF-10-Catalyzed 1,5-Enyne Cycloisomerization Reaction
To a $2\mathsf{m L}$ vial was added $\mathsf{I P r A u(l i l)S b F}_{6}$ -IRMOF-10 ( $16\%$ IPrAu(BPDC)Cl loading, 0.03 equiv) immersed in DCM $(0.3~\mathrm{mL})$ , followed by the addition of 1,5-enyne (1 equiv). After $22\mathsf{h}$ , the organic supernatant was removed with DCM ( $2\mathsf{m L}\times5)$ . The washed $1\mathsf{P r A u}(111)\mathsf{S b}\mathsf{F}_{6}$ -IRMOF-10 crystals were resubjected to the same conditions for recyclability studies. Conversions were determined by $^1\mathsf{H}$ NMR spectroscopy. No additional conversion was detected in the supernatant upon removal of IPrAu(III) ${\mathsf{S b F}}_{6}$ -IRMOF-10. $^1\mathsf{H}$ NMR spectra of products 2 and 6 match those previously reported.29 For control experiments, an equivalent amount of $\mathsf{I P r A u}(\mathsf{I I I})\mathsf{C}\mathsf{I}$ -IRMOF10 or IRMOF-9 was used instead of $1\mathsf{P r A u}(111)\mathsf{S b F}_{6}$ -IRMOF-10. $14\%$ loading IPrAu(BPDC)Cl versus BPDC was observed by digestion $^1\mathsf{H}$ NMR analysis for IPrAu(III)SbF $_6$ -IRMOF-10 after catalysis. Zn:Au ratio of 88:12 observed for IPrAu(III) ${\mathsf{S b F}}_{6}$ -IRMOF-10 by ICP-AES after catalysis.
